================================================================================
Vendored TLS stack (`vendor/leyline-ssl/`, `vendor/leyline-ssl-sys/`,
`vendor/tokio-leyline-ssl/`)
================================================================================

The vendored BoringSSL Rust bindings are derived from `0x676e67/boring2`
(https://github.com/0x676e67/boring2), which is itself a fork of Cloudflare's
`boring` crate (https://github.com/cloudflare/boring).

The TLS-extension work that makes browser fingerprinting possible —
in particular MLKEM768 key agreement, ALPS, deterministic GREASE wiring,
and cipher/extension ordering hooks — originates in `boring2`.

Licenses: Apache-2.0 and MIT, dual-licensed per upstream. License files
preserved in `vendor/leyline-ssl/LICENSE`, `vendor/leyline-ssl-sys/LICENSE-MIT`,
and `vendor/tokio-leyline-ssl/LICENSE-{APACHE,MIT}`.

Original authors (non-exhaustive):
- Alex Crichton <alex@alexcrichton.com>
- Steven Fackler <sfackler@gmail.com>
- Ivan Nikulin <ifaaan@gmail.com>
- Jack Lloyd

================================================================================
Vendored BoringSSL (`vendor/leyline-ssl-sys/deps/boringssl/`)
================================================================================

BoringSSL is a fork of OpenSSL maintained by Google. Large parts fall under
OpenSSL licensing; files that are wholly new carry a Google copyright and an
ISC license. The full text is preserved at
`vendor/leyline-ssl-sys/deps/boringssl/LICENSE`.

Third-party components inside BoringSSL retain their own licenses, notably:
- `src/third_party/fiat/` (MIT)
- `src/third_party/googletest/` (BSD-3-Clause) — used only by upstream tests

================================================================================
Vendored BoringSSL patches (`vendor/leyline-ssl-sys/patches/`)
================================================================================

- `boring-pq.patch` — post-quantum key agreements (MLKEM768, Kyber draft
  codepoints). Authored by Bas Westerbaan <bas@cloudflare.com>, Cloudflare,
  commit `b98d803dbecc9d6848d8cbffa62b5c943fb75f70`, 2022-07-22.
- `underscore-wildcards.patch` — permit underscores in DNS wildcards under
  `X509_CHECK_FLAG_UNDERSCORE_WILDCARDS`. Cloudflare BoringSSL branch
  (`cloudflare:boringssl:underscore-wildcards`).
- `boringssl-loongarch.patch` — LoongArch architecture support.
  Authored by WANG Rui <wangrui@loongson.cn>, commit
  `d39506c373dc03b1bfab2c01abc2232e36d13ed6`, 2025-04-27.

